---
import EntryArticle from "../components/EntryArticle.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<EntryArticle
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site does with personal data."
  page="entry privacy"
  meta={["Last updated 26 October 2026"]}
>
  <p>
    This is the personal website of {site.name}, based in {site.location}, Belgium. You can reach me at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form, I receive the name, email address and message you type. The form is
    processed by Formspree (Formspree, Inc., United States), which forwards it to my inbox. I use these
    details only to reply to you and keep them only as long as needed to handle your message. The legal
    basis is my legitimate interest in answering you (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)).
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies and has no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts. Fonts are served from
    this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Other parties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The site is hosted by Netlify, which may keep technical server logs (such as your IP address) to
      deliver and secure the site.
    </li>
    <li>
      The running chart is embedded from cedrichelewaut.github.io (GitHub Pages), which receives your IP
      address when the chart loads.
    </li>
    <li>Links to LinkedIn, GitHub and Instagram are plain links. Those services only see you once you follow them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask me to access, correct or delete the data I hold about you, or object to its use, by
    emailing me. You can also lodge a complaint with the Belgian Data Protection Authority
    (<a href="https://www.gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit.be" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit.be</a
    >).
  </p>
</EntryArticle>
